# Supabase Configuration
# Get these values from your Supabase project dashboard:
# 1. Go to https://supabase.com and create a new project
# 2. Navigate to Settings > API
# 3. Copy the Project URL and anon public key
# 4. Replace the values below (remove the placeholder text)

# Example: https://abcdefghijklmnop.supabase.co
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=your_actual_supabase_project_url_here

# Example: eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9...
EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your_actual_supabase_anon_key_here

# AccuWeather API Configuration
# Get your free API key at: https://developer.accuweather.com/
# Free tier provides 50 API calls per day
EXPO_PUBLIC_ACCUWEATHER_API_KEY=your_accuweather_api_key_here

# IMPORTANT: 
# - Do NOT include quotes around the values
# - Do NOT add extra spaces
# - Make sure the URL starts with https://
# - The anon key should be a long string starting with eyJ
# - The app will use mock weather data if no AccuWeather API key is provided
# - Mock data includes enhanced mountain weather conditions for Mount Babag